  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough Saturday...\n\nConditions trend warmer and drier into Tuesday as the area \nremains situated under northwest flow aloft, with ridging to the \nwest, and upper troughing to the east. Occasional weak waves will \ndrop through the periphery of the area bringing isolated shower \nand weak thunderstorm chances, mainly for east/northeast areas. \nBreezy winds will be found over the east on Monday, with northwest\nwind gusts of 20-40 mph expected, strongest near the Dakotas \nborder. Winds increase on Tuesday, ahead of a stronger shortwave\nexpected to drop into the region Tuesday night/Wednesday. \nWesterly winds will be strongest over the western foothills\nTuesday, with lesser winds to the east. There are currently \nmoderate probabilities for wind gusts to 50 mph along the western\nfoothills. As the aforementioned wave and associated cold front \ndrop through the region Tuesday night/Wednesday, breezy northwest \nwinds are expected to spread over the entire area, strongest over \nthe far east and down along the east side of the Bighorns \n(moderate chance of wind gusts to 50 mph). Wind highlites are not \nanticipated for Tuesday or Wednesday at this time, though it is \nsomething to monitor. Cooler conditions can be expected for \nWednesday behind the front, along with a better potential for \nshowers/thunderstorms (20-60% chance) into Wednesday night, mainly\nfor northern and eastern areas.\n\nOccasional pieces of energy will continue to move through\nnorthwest flow through the end of the work week, allowing \nisolated afternoon/evening showers and thunderstorms to continue\n(20% or less chance). Ensembles continue to indicate upper \ntroughing will move onto the West Coast Friday into Saturday, with\nsouthwest flow developing over the northern Rockies. This would \nbring a better potential for daily thunderstorms over the upcoming\nweekend with shortwaves lifting into the region and plains\nmoisture advecting into the area.\n\nHigh temperatures are forecast to range from the 70s to lower 80s\nMonday, to the 80s Tuesday. Temperatures cool down to near normal\nWednesday through Saturday with highs in the 70s to near 80\ndegrees. STP",
